What failed:
`KeyboardInnerHandle::set_focus` sent `wl_keyboard.leave` to the old focus while modifiers were held, with no `wl_keyboard.modifiers` clearing them. A client that pressed Super and then lost the focus to a compositor shortcut (Super+Tab, Super+A opening a panel) never saw Super come up; clients that keep their state across a leave (X11 apps through Xwayland, games) acted as if it were still held (owner report 2026-11-15; AUDIT_INPUT_LIFECYCLE finding 1).

Change:
Before the old focus leaves (focus replaced or unset), when any modifier is depressed or latched, it gets one `modifiers` event with depressed and latched cleared; locked modifiers (Caps Lock, Num Lock) and the layout are kept. The new focus gets the real state on enter as before.

Owner decision and date:
Owner report 2026-11-15; applied the same day (commit 4ee7076).

Upstream status:
Not sent; no reason recorded. Whether Smithay `master` does this was not verified (its
`set_focus` was not read in full on 2026-11-26).

